# Review requirements for the paths that can cause a destructive false positive.
#
# The rule catalog decides which folders, processes, registry keys and signed applications get
# deleted from a user's machine. No rule change is auto-merged (see
# puakiller-ai-architecture-kit/DECISIONS.md), and every path below needs a named reviewer.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @ZER0Nep

# The source of truth for detection and removal.
/rules/                 @ZER0Nep

# Machine-generated proposals. Inert by design -- nothing compiles them -- but this is where a
# review that skipped a step would be least visible, so it needs a named reviewer like any
# other path that can end in a deletion rule.
/rules/proposed/        @ZER0Nep

# The scripts that ship to end users. Their rule region is generated from /rules/catalog.json;
# hand-editing it is caught by scripts/verify-generated.py in CI.
/hosted-removal.ps1     @ZER0Nep
/PUAKILLER-LOCAL.ps1    @ZER0Nep

# The compiler and the gate that guards the generated region.
/scripts/               @ZER0Nep

# The false-positive and detection corpora. Weakening a benign corpus is how a safe rule
# quietly becomes a destructive one.
/tests/                 @ZER0Nep

# CI permissions, and the workflow that holds a write token.
/.github/               @ZER0Nep
